# The Gradle wrapper, spelled out rather than left to auto-detection.
#
# gradlew is a shell script that Linux runs directly, so it must keep LF
# endings whatever the machine that committed it uses -- a CRLF gradlew
# fails on CI with "bad interpreter", which is a confusing way to find
# out about line endings.
#
# The jar is binary and must never be touched by any conversion at all.
gradlew            text eol=lf
gradlew.bat        text eol=crlf
gradle-wrapper.jar binary
